  "explicit_limitations": [
    "Failure to find a refuting observation corroborates an action only relative to LLM-proposed suspicions St and available read APIs; it is not a formal safety proof.",
    "Algorithm 1 Line 13 executes the fourth draft even if blocked after 3 redrafts to prevent infinite loops, requiring hard blocks or human approval for irreversible production writes.",
    "Verification increases API token cost by 1.5x to 9.4x over ReAct (e.g., $0.447 vs. $0.047 on thinking-on Qwen3.5-27B challenge; 54.4% rejection rate), though disabling thinking reduces challenge tokens from 22.9k to 7.3k at 81.5% TGC.",
    "Under genuinely ambiguous user instructions, Section 6 notes BlackSwan repeatedly raises the same unresolved suspicion across redrafts without resolving intent.",
    "AppWorld, WebShop, and ALFWorld are deterministic simulated sandboxes with clean read-only primitives; non-Qwen3.5-27B rows in Table 8 are single runs, MiniMax/GLM baselines use 3-demo prompts vs. 1-demo BlackSwan, ACCORD was reimplemented due to missing code as of Sept 2026, and WebShop Prompts 11/12 encode shop termination semantics."
  ],
